00:46:44.870 --> 00:46:47.110
A lot of times, for me,

00:46:47.110 --> 00:46:49.434
when I hear about somebody
who did something stupid

00:46:49.434 --> 00:46:52.818
or something wrong that happened,

00:46:52.818 --> 00:46:54.735
I immediately add it to

00:46:56.074 --> 00:47:01.058
my big bag of things that
I'm supposed to figure out.

00:47:01.058 --> 00:47:03.544
So that's why occasionally I'll write

00:47:03.544 --> 00:47:06.364
one of these medium pieces
about some issue, right?

00:47:06.364 --> 00:47:07.625
And it's because my personality is

00:47:07.625 --> 00:47:10.963
is if you give me this information,

00:47:10.963 --> 00:47:14.181
I feel responsible for
having an opinion about it.

00:47:14.181 --> 00:47:16.130
And then sometimes that responsibility

00:47:16.130 --> 00:47:19.069
for having an opinion
because of my platform

00:47:19.069 --> 00:47:22.345
translates into, you have
to say something about this.

00:47:22.345 --> 00:47:24.015
Like, it is your responsibility

00:47:24.015 --> 00:47:26.848
to speak your perspective on this.

00:47:28.872 --> 00:47:31.227
And that's probably based on narcissism

00:47:31.227 --> 00:47:33.834
and thinking that my perspective
is important, whatever,

00:47:33.834 --> 00:47:36.404
but it is based on my sense of justice

00:47:36.404 --> 00:47:40.361
and feeling like I need to say something.

00:47:40.361 --> 00:47:42.941
But what I was realizing is that

00:47:42.941 --> 00:47:45.712
she's telling me about something
that the president said

00:47:45.712 --> 00:47:47.962
or something that happened.

00:47:49.136 --> 00:47:51.958
And it's just adding to this bag of stuff

00:47:51.958 --> 00:47:54.730
that I feel like I have to process.

00:47:54.730 --> 00:47:57.014
And I told my therapist,

00:47:57.014 --> 00:47:59.514
I feel like for this month of,

00:48:00.472 --> 00:48:02.749
that we're moving into June,

00:48:02.749 --> 00:48:06.052
I'm gonna kind of take a news fast

00:48:06.052 --> 00:48:09.347
and not feel like I have to be informed

00:48:09.347 --> 00:48:10.976
about every single thing that's happening

00:48:10.976 --> 00:48:12.572
with the virus or every single thing

00:48:12.572 --> 00:48:15.054
that the president is saying or doing,

00:48:15.054 --> 00:48:17.554
like just sort of for a second

00:48:18.519 --> 00:48:21.498
turn that faucet off
and see how it affects

00:48:21.498 --> 00:48:24.350
my personal health and perspective.

00:48:24.350 --> 00:48:25.904
Because a lot of times,
even before eating,

00:48:25.904 --> 00:48:28.429
when I get up in the morning
and I'm about to meditate,

00:48:28.429 --> 00:48:29.612
if I've gone on Twitter

00:48:29.612 --> 00:48:32.945
and I've seen the latest bullshit thing,

00:48:34.455 --> 00:48:36.125
is I take that into that process

00:48:36.125 --> 00:48:37.636
and it's very difficult to let go of.

00:48:37.636 --> 00:48:38.489
Yeah.

00:48:38.489 --> 00:48:40.072
So in that sense,

00:48:41.499 --> 00:48:43.399
what I'm getting at in
answer to this question is

00:48:43.399 --> 00:48:47.732
I feel like to a certain
degree, ignorance is bliss.

00:48:49.845 --> 00:48:52.873
Yeah, I mean, I think it's
clear in this situation

00:48:52.873 --> 00:48:55.595
that the key is moderation.

00:48:55.595 --> 00:48:57.928
I mean, welcome to my world.

00:48:59.089 --> 00:49:02.339
I err on the opposite side of just not,

00:49:03.383 --> 00:49:05.874
of being more ignorant about
things that are happening.

00:49:05.874 --> 00:49:07.718
I mean, when you talk
about news especially,

00:49:07.718 --> 00:49:10.287
it's like, it gets to
me in a different way

00:49:10.287 --> 00:49:15.287
because I feel like, I think
you have this sense of like,

00:49:15.337 --> 00:49:18.393
because there's something that you can do,

00:49:18.393 --> 00:49:19.822
whether it's the fact
that we have a platform

00:49:19.822 --> 00:49:23.264
or the fact that you enjoy writing

00:49:23.264 --> 00:49:24.667
and piecing things together.

00:49:24.667 --> 00:49:29.084
So you do have an outlet to
weigh in on these things.

00:49:31.299 --> 00:49:33.056
I actually feel personally

00:49:33.056 --> 00:49:36.973
because that I don't have
that same experience,

00:49:38.230 --> 00:49:42.046
I feel a frustration and
kind of a helplessness

00:49:42.046 --> 00:49:43.350
when those things happen,

00:49:43.350 --> 00:49:46.100
so it's not a pressure to engage.

00:49:48.503 --> 00:49:51.493
It's a frustration that I just don't feel

00:49:51.493 --> 00:49:53.910
like I'm equipped to do that.

00:49:55.380 --> 00:49:57.971
I feel that sometimes.

00:49:57.971 --> 00:50:02.054
But then if I get bombarded
with a lot of things,

00:50:02.971 --> 00:50:03.888
I have this

00:50:06.089 --> 00:50:08.339
palpable sense of capacity.

00:50:10.396 --> 00:50:12.913
You talk about things accumulating

00:50:12.913 --> 00:50:14.906
and it just kind of builds up,

00:50:14.906 --> 00:50:17.156
to me, it's not a pressure.

00:50:18.113 --> 00:50:21.086
Its a, I just get buried underneath it

00:50:21.086 --> 00:50:24.258
and I feel like I can't
do the things that I want,

00:50:24.258 --> 00:50:28.835
that I do need to devote
my energy and attention to.

00:50:28.835 --> 00:50:31.492
And to a fault, right?

00:50:31.492 --> 00:50:34.030
So there are times when there's
certain things in the news

00:50:34.030 --> 00:50:36.144
that I do need to know about

00:50:36.144 --> 00:50:38.384
and at least be exposed to it.

00:50:38.384 --> 00:50:40.440
Maybe I don't have to have an opinion

00:50:40.440 --> 00:50:45.217
that then I would publicly
lay in somebody about it,

00:50:45.217 --> 00:50:46.050
but it is,

00:50:48.089 --> 00:50:50.966
it's good and it's healthy to understand

00:50:50.966 --> 00:50:53.167
what's happening out there again,

00:50:53.167 --> 00:50:55.750
to just stay on the news front.

00:50:58.516 --> 00:50:59.599
So, I try to,

00:51:01.302 --> 00:51:03.669
like I'll listen to Up First,

00:51:03.669 --> 00:51:05.919
which is like a very quick,

00:51:07.134 --> 00:51:09.046
like the headlines, you know,

00:51:09.046 --> 00:51:11.213
it just kind of takes
you through the headlines

00:51:11.213 --> 00:51:14.150
and then you move on, but I'm
not reading these articles

00:51:14.150 --> 00:51:18.759
and like getting really
deep in a lot of things.

00:51:18.759 --> 00:51:20.505
So that's been my correction

00:51:20.505 --> 00:51:22.053
is I need to be a little bit more,

00:51:22.053 --> 00:51:24.251
I need to be a little
less ignorant about things

00:51:24.251 --> 00:51:25.334
because yes,

00:51:27.037 --> 00:51:30.012
I think it does simplify my life

00:51:30.012 --> 00:51:32.912
and it gives me the capacity
to invest in the things

00:51:32.912 --> 00:51:34.137
I need to invest in,

00:51:34.137 --> 00:51:35.896
but there's some things
that come in sideways

00:51:35.896 --> 00:51:39.738
that you didn't anticipate that
you need to be informed by.

00:51:39.738 --> 00:51:42.922
And so I've made some
adjustments on that level,

00:51:42.922 --> 00:51:44.675
but in this day and age,

00:51:44.675 --> 00:51:48.175
I try not to get too deep in it, because--

00:51:49.014 --> 00:51:53.259
Well, and I think it's personality based.

00:51:53.259 --> 00:51:55.112
It's very personality based.

00:51:55.112 --> 00:51:57.240
For instance, okay,

00:51:57.240 --> 00:52:01.525
those of you who follow me
on Instagram or Twitter,

00:52:01.525 --> 00:52:05.961
know that first of all,
I'm incredibly sporadic

00:52:05.961 --> 00:52:08.767
and sometimes I'll just
go on a run for a few days

00:52:08.767 --> 00:52:11.703
or a few weeks where I'm pretty
active on those platforms.

00:52:11.703 --> 00:52:14.842
And it's usually an
indication that I don't,

00:52:14.842 --> 00:52:19.592
we don't have a project that's
taking a lot of bulk time.

00:52:21.019 --> 00:52:24.645
And at the very beginning of quarantine,

00:52:24.645 --> 00:52:27.780
we had a lot of time all of a sudden,

00:52:27.780 --> 00:52:29.739
because our lives were turned upside down

00:52:29.739 --> 00:52:31.949
and our business was turned upside down.

00:52:31.949 --> 00:52:34.197
And then, you know, I
get really frustrated

00:52:34.197 --> 00:52:39.197
when I just see people spouting
off things that aren't true.

00:52:39.205 --> 00:52:43.538
And there's been so much
misinformation around COVID

00:52:44.547 --> 00:52:46.875
and it's like, people
just fall into two camps

00:52:46.875 --> 00:52:51.708
and they don't, it's like
everything has become political.

00:52:52.605 --> 00:52:56.469
And so I, and listen, I'm no authority.

00:52:56.469 --> 00:52:58.104
And I try to say that over and over again.

00:52:58.104 --> 00:52:59.870
I'm just a dude who's
interested in this stuff

00:52:59.870 --> 00:53:04.110
who has a platform, who
makes a living on YouTube.

00:53:04.110 --> 00:53:06.029
So I'm definitely not an
authority on any of this,

00:53:06.029 --> 00:53:09.919
but I like to point and sort
of elevate voices that are,

00:53:09.919 --> 00:53:12.974
point to voices that are authorities.

00:53:12.974 --> 00:53:16.803
And, you know, I went through this phase

00:53:16.803 --> 00:53:18.322
where I was kind of like engaging.

00:53:18.322 --> 00:53:19.155
I was posting something

00:53:19.155 --> 00:53:20.773
and the people would like
have questions about it

00:53:20.773 --> 00:53:23.829
or be critical of it and
I would personally engage.

00:53:23.829 --> 00:53:25.752
And you may notice, well,
I haven't been doing that

00:53:25.752 --> 00:53:28.689
for the past few weeks and it's largely,

00:53:28.689 --> 00:53:30.692
I mean, there's a number of reasons.

00:53:30.692 --> 00:53:33.185
One is we are busy with other things.

00:53:33.185 --> 00:53:35.425
There is a couple of
things that are taking more

00:53:35.425 --> 00:53:39.024
like bulk pieces of my
time, more attention.

00:53:39.024 --> 00:53:41.507
There's also a sense of
hopelessness, you know?

00:53:41.507 --> 00:53:43.626
There's this sense that like,

00:53:43.626 --> 00:53:46.555
there are just some people
who are so committed to,

00:53:46.555 --> 00:53:50.358
they're just dug in their trench so deeply

00:53:50.358 --> 00:53:53.168
that nothing that you can say

00:53:53.168 --> 00:53:54.864
and no fact that you can point them to

00:53:54.864 --> 00:53:55.804
is gonna change anything

00:53:55.804 --> 00:53:58.689
and so there just becomes
a sense of hopelessness.

00:53:58.689 --> 00:54:00.804
And so I've kind of backed off that

00:54:00.804 --> 00:54:03.623
and then the thing that
I'm adding to it is.

00:54:03.623 --> 00:54:04.979
Well, I also don't even
want to really know

00:54:04.979 --> 00:54:06.603
what's happening in the
news for a little bit,

00:54:06.603 --> 00:54:08.323
just for my own personal health.

00:54:08.323 --> 00:54:12.671
But I am very grateful to
the people who day by day,

00:54:12.671 --> 00:54:15.401
especially those people who are
authorities on these issues.

00:54:15.401 --> 00:54:16.948
And there are a few
people I follow on Twitter

00:54:16.948 --> 00:54:20.365
who are like a daily briefing about COVID

00:54:21.547 --> 00:54:23.857
and here's the latest, you know,

00:54:23.857 --> 00:54:26.584
or you've got certain websites like Snopes

00:54:26.584 --> 00:54:29.834
that are committed to
setting the record straight

00:54:29.834 --> 00:54:31.077
on all these issues

00:54:31.077 --> 00:54:34.416
and they're constantly having
to deal with misinformation.

00:54:34.416 --> 00:54:36.707
I just am very grateful to those people

00:54:36.707 --> 00:54:39.561
who are in the trenches
and fighting that battle

00:54:39.561 --> 00:54:42.539
and trying to fight this information

00:54:42.539 --> 00:54:45.372
and get the right information out,

00:54:46.415 --> 00:54:48.171
but I just, I can't do it.

00:54:48.171 --> 00:54:49.760
It's just not, it's not healthy to do it,

00:54:49.760 --> 00:54:53.064
but like you said, there
are some things, you know,

00:54:53.064 --> 00:54:54.834
like what happened with Ahmaud Arbery

00:54:54.834 --> 00:54:57.364
or what happened when
we're recording this,

00:54:57.364 --> 00:54:59.685
just happened two days ago,

00:54:59.685 --> 00:55:02.820
two days ago in Minneapolis
with George Floyd.

00:55:02.820 --> 00:55:06.912
And I'll put something on
Instagram or Twitter about that,

00:55:06.912 --> 00:55:10.498
just to acknowledge that, you know, again,

00:55:10.498 --> 00:55:12.825
I want to elevate those voices,

00:55:12.825 --> 00:55:17.393
and I want to bring attention
to something with my platform.

00:55:17.393 --> 00:55:19.115
I'm not trying to pontificate

00:55:19.115 --> 00:55:20.900
or come in and try to
say something about it.

00:55:20.900 --> 00:55:22.125
I'm just more like this is a thing

00:55:22.125 --> 00:55:24.375
that you should know about.

00:55:26.463 --> 00:55:27.981
So like you said, there's a balance

00:55:27.981 --> 00:55:31.398
because I don't want to completely detach

00:55:32.996 --> 00:55:35.117
because there's so much injustice

00:55:35.117 --> 00:55:38.253
and there's so much misinformation

00:55:38.253 --> 00:55:39.883
that's constantly just happening

00:55:39.883 --> 00:55:41.966
that if you have a platform,

00:55:41.966 --> 00:55:44.650
I feel like you've got to
be engaged on some level

00:55:44.650 --> 00:55:46.738
Or, I mean, not even a platform.

00:55:46.738 --> 00:55:51.321
I think for me, it's like,
I know we're very fortunate.

00:55:52.484 --> 00:55:56.076
Hashtag blessed, you know, in so many ways

00:55:56.076 --> 00:55:58.520
and we're privileged, right?

00:55:58.520 --> 00:55:59.520
And it's not

00:56:01.010 --> 00:56:03.510
necessarily just, and so it's,

00:56:04.997 --> 00:56:08.164
I can live in this bubble of ignorance

00:56:09.531 --> 00:56:12.281
and be blissful and it's in this.

00:56:13.154 --> 00:56:16.850
And if you take that too far, it's I just,

00:56:16.850 --> 00:56:18.159
I don't want to be that person.

00:56:18.159 --> 00:56:20.383
And it's just not right to say, okay,

00:56:20.383 --> 00:56:22.133
as long as I'm happy,

00:56:23.246 --> 00:56:24.413
then I'm good.

00:56:25.856 --> 00:56:28.576
It's very self centered.

00:56:28.576 --> 00:56:31.826
Now, to take that to an extreme, right?

00:56:32.710 --> 00:56:35.363
But you also have to know
what your limits are.

00:56:35.363 --> 00:56:37.240
and I think that's what
we're talking about.

00:56:37.240 --> 00:56:38.945
So it's not, I'm going to check out

00:56:38.945 --> 00:56:43.272
and I'm going to do whatever
it takes for me to be happy.

00:56:43.272 --> 00:56:47.839
I don't want my actions to
just be about my happiness

00:56:47.839 --> 00:56:51.266
or just the people that I love the most,

00:56:51.266 --> 00:56:54.528
because I know them or
I'm related to them,

00:56:54.528 --> 00:56:57.047
it's like, you want to--

00:56:57.047 --> 00:56:57.960
Well and there's a way to--

00:56:57.960 --> 00:57:02.960
I wanna extend myself and that
starts with being informed.

00:57:03.514 --> 00:57:04.594
And there's a way to be informed--

00:57:04.594 --> 00:57:05.821
You cant fight every battle,

00:57:05.821 --> 00:57:09.247
but if you're not fighting any battles,

00:57:09.247 --> 00:57:13.202
at least I don't feel like
that's the right choice for me.

00:57:13.202 --> 00:57:14.684
Well, and there's a way to be informed

00:57:14.684 --> 00:57:18.838
that doesn't take all your
time like you're saying.

00:57:18.838 --> 00:57:22.088
I think one of the things that helps me

00:57:23.395 --> 00:57:26.558
and I'm not, you know, I'm not organized,

00:57:26.558 --> 00:57:30.308
but I am very like goal
oriented task driven.

00:57:33.114 --> 00:57:34.721
And one of the things that helps me

00:57:34.721 --> 00:57:39.531
with just getting all the
things that I do done is like,

00:57:39.531 --> 00:57:41.198
okay, here's the day.

00:57:41.198 --> 00:57:42.176
This is what I got.

00:57:42.176 --> 00:57:43.537
I'm gonna actually,

00:57:43.537 --> 00:57:46.208
I'd like to get this
much of this thing done

00:57:46.208 --> 00:57:48.375
and I'd like to get this
much of this thing done

00:57:48.375 --> 00:57:49.532
and I kind of got a vision

00:57:49.532 --> 00:57:51.290
for what that day's gonna look like.

00:57:51.290 --> 00:57:52.662
And then I kind of do it

00:57:52.662 --> 00:57:55.451
and I cut myself some slack
if I don't quite get there,

00:57:55.451 --> 00:57:59.316
but at least I kind of
know where I'm gonna go.

00:57:59.316 --> 00:58:02.646
And then when it comes to
stuff like social media,

00:58:02.646 --> 00:58:05.186
even if you're going on to Twitter

00:58:05.186 --> 00:58:07.467
with the intention of figuring out

00:58:07.467 --> 00:58:08.608
what's going on in the world,

00:58:08.608 --> 00:58:10.317
is there any news that
I need to know about,

00:58:10.317 --> 00:58:13.400
should I be informed about something?

00:58:15.360 --> 00:58:17.863
It's it's one thing to just basically

00:58:17.863 --> 00:58:19.334
constantly go back in there

00:58:19.334 --> 00:58:21.575
every time you get a little bit bored.

00:58:21.575 --> 00:58:24.149
And then when you learn about an issue,

00:58:24.149 --> 00:58:26.350
kind of go down that rabbit hole

00:58:26.350 --> 00:58:28.770
and start arguing with somebody
on the internet about it

00:58:28.770 --> 00:58:31.139
or finding every perspective on it.

00:58:31.139 --> 00:58:32.567
And then the next thing you know,

00:58:32.567 --> 00:58:35.065
you spent two hours on your phone

00:58:35.065 --> 00:58:37.225
and you've accomplished nothing.

00:58:37.225 --> 00:58:39.474
That's one thing and then
it's another thing to be like,

00:58:39.474 --> 00:58:41.963
I want to know about this.

00:58:41.963 --> 00:58:43.698
It's like with you know,

00:58:43.698 --> 00:58:45.121
I kind of checked out yesterday,

00:58:45.121 --> 00:58:48.038
didn't pay attention to much stuff.

00:58:49.148 --> 00:58:50.941
That's another thing I didn't mention,

00:58:50.941 --> 00:58:52.812
when I got home, all that stuff happened

00:58:52.812 --> 00:58:57.395
with my kids and my wife,
but in the middle of all that

00:58:58.364 --> 00:59:00.604
I stepped outside and went on Twitter

00:59:00.604 --> 00:59:05.104
and that's when I saw the
George Floyd video and I got

00:59:06.411 --> 00:59:07.650
very angry.

00:59:07.650 --> 00:59:11.562
I just was, I was so angry about that.

00:59:11.562 --> 00:59:15.229
And then of course, all
I did was just post,

00:59:17.281 --> 00:59:18.606
I think this morning actually

00:59:18.606 --> 00:59:22.516
just post a picture of him on my Instagram

00:59:22.516 --> 00:59:26.352
and it's like, I'm sure I could do more--

00:59:26.352 --> 00:59:29.430
And I didn't find out
about it until this morning

00:59:29.430 --> 00:59:34.430
when I had my slot where I was
like catching up on the news.

00:59:37.622 --> 00:59:41.865
And I wouldn't want to
never have known about it

00:59:41.865 --> 00:59:44.528
and for it to impact me the
way that it did this morning

00:59:44.528 --> 00:59:47.528
'cause it certainly did and it does.

00:59:48.719 --> 00:59:51.400
But it didn't last night
because I set up parameters

00:59:51.400 --> 00:59:54.417
and there were things I was invested in

00:59:54.417 --> 00:59:56.626
last night with my family.

00:59:56.626 --> 00:59:59.450
I think we can leave it at that, right?

00:59:59.450 --> 01:00:03.943
I wanted to switch gears
to one more question.

01:00:03.943 --> 01:00:06.110
Cat, @Chinalinkster, okay.

01:00:07.390 --> 01:00:09.654
You can use my picture if you want to.

01:00:09.654 --> 01:00:13.464
Could a snake physically wear clothes?

01:00:13.464 --> 01:00:14.486
